WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.069
-Joe Biden met Russian
President Vladimir Putin

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:06.439
face-to-face for the first time
in his presidency

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.840
during a summit in Geneva.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.576
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:13.913 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.014
Biden has been on the first

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.116
major international trip
of his presidency,

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.185
meeting with leaders
of the G7 and NATO

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:22.088
and trying to restore
our relationship with key allies

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.323
who seemed excited to have
a U.S. President

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.525
interested in global cooperation
on issues

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:28.694
like climate and the pandemic,
as opposed to the last guy

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:31.964
who openly professed
his admiration for dictators.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:33.900
But when it came time
to meet with a U.S. ally,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.035
he always had
the bummed-out look of a guy

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.138
who was in a waiting room
at a urologist's office.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:41.007
Looks like he should be flipping
through an old "Golf Digest,"

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.143
getting mad whenever
someone else's name is called.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.312
"Okay, he definitely came in
after me. This is bull[bleep]"

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.048
Trump was always visibly
thrilled to meet with Putin

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.484
or Mohammed bin Salman
or Kim Jong-un.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.286
But then when he had to sit down
with Angela Merkel,

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.854
he looked like he got dragged
into the principal's office

00:00:55.854 --> 00:00:58.290
for setting some goats loose
in the parking lot

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.725
on senior prank day.

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:02.094
"Do you know how much
property damage you caused?"

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:03.495
"But it was all in good fun."

00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:05.064
"You don't even go
to this school."

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.733
"That's all part
of the prank, man."

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:10.403
U.S. allies seem to be
enjoying the change of pace.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.305
And, in particular, Biden really
seems to be chumming it up

00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:15.241
with French President
Emmanuel Macron,

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.044
meeting one-on-one with him
in wicker chairs by the beach

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.913
like they were doing press
for one of those

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.481
Nicole Kidman
seaside murder dramas,

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:24.583
talking intensely
as other G7 leaders

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:25.685
walked alongside them.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.186
And chatting again later

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.054
during a more informal
gathering,

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:31.123
Macron looks like
he's reenacting

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.292
all the weird [bleep]
Trump ever did to him.

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.062
"And then he brushed dandruff
off my shoulder

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.363
and asked me if I could show him

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.333
where they make
the French's mustard."

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.035
Thanks to their age difference,
Biden looks like a dad

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:45.171
giving his adult son
financial advice.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.673
"You got to start saving
for retirement now.

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:48.942
Get a Roth IRA.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.143
How much did you spend
on this suit?

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:53.146
I got a guy who will
make you one for 50 bucks.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.982
He just cuts it out
of the carpet in his house."

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.983
But, of course,
the biggest test so far,

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:00.185
just how much American
leadership on the world stage

00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:01.887
has changed in the post-Trump
era, came today

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:03.789
when Biden met Putin
face-to-face.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.258
Ahead of the meeting,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.461
Biden declared that he'd be
holding a solo press conference

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.762
rather than doing one
with Putin,

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.564
a change from the Trump years.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.901
-The bottom line is that I think
the best way to deal with this

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:18.737
is for he and I to meet,
he and I to have our discussion.

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:22.274
I know you don't doubt that
I'll be very straightforward

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:25.244
[laughs] with him
about our concerns.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:28.814
And I will make clear my view
of how that meeting turned out.

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:32.952
And he'll make clear, from his
perspective, how it turned out.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:37.056
But I don't want
to get into being diverted

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:41.860
by, "Did they shake hands?
How far -- Who talked the most?"

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:45.331
-First of all, we know
who'd do most of the talking.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.700
It's Biden.
In any situation, it's Biden.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.203
If Biden went on a tour
of the Sistine Chapel

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.738
where they tell you not to talk,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.606
he'd make it five seconds
before saying,

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.474
"How the hell
do you paint a ceiling

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:56.843
without it dripping
all over you?

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.544
I got to get
the number of their guy.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:03.516
What? I'm not talking.
I'm asking a question."

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.218
Also, Putin doesn't talk.
He glares.

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:08.554
Biden would be 10 minutes
into an answer on sanctions

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.590
while Putin just
sits there silently,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.959
either hatching a plan
for world domination

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.862
or rehearsing judo moves
in his head.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:19.298
"Gonna do some jogging with
the knees low -- low knees --

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:20.700
and then trot, trot, trot

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.503
and then a roll-over
and then hop up

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:27.740
and then go into a slow roll
like a baby, back to my feet.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.476
Slow roll like a baby,
back to my feet.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.778
And then maybe a little
prance, prance, prance.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:33.980
Prance and dance.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.983
And I'm going to flip you
to the ground like boom.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.318
And that is how that will go."

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.421
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.293
Of course, no one even asked
questions about handshakes

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.329
or talking during Trump's
meeting with Putin in Helsinki,

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:53.899
given that there were much
stranger moments to dissect,

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:55.868
like when Putin gave Trump
a soccer ball

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:59.371
and Trump definitely looked like
he didn't know what it was.

00:03:59.371 --> 00:04:03.842
"I guess in Russia, they bowl
without the finger holes."

00:04:03.842 --> 00:04:06.745
Back then, the questions
came from Trump himself,

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:09.715
and they were a little more
along the lines of crazy old man

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:11.383
waiting for his check
at a diner.

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:12.952
-Where is the server?

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.121
I want to know,
where is the server,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.856
and what is the server saying?

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:20.226
I really do want
to see the server.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.061
What happened to the server?

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.063
-Remember that, when the
President of the United States

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.865
used a press conference
with the leader

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.133
of a foreign adversary
to complain in length

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.503
about an insane conspiracy
theory involving a server?

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:33.205
He sounded like he was waiting
for his jalapeño poppers

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:35.207
at Applebee's.
"I ordered them 10 minutes ago.

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:37.510
Where is the server?

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.112
I need my poppers.
I got to get my pop on."

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:41.980
And, you know, honestly,
side note here --

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.949
I do think that would be
a great catchphrase

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.284
for an Applebee's commercial.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.253
I mean, can you picture a guy,
settles into a table,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.655
orders a steaming-hot plate
of jalapeño poppers,

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:52.124
then he looks straight down the
barrel of the camera and says,

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:53.993
"I got to get my pop on"?

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.963
It's certainly much better than

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:00.132
"eatin' good
in the neighborhood."

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:02.501
Just because it rhymes,
it doesn't mean it makes sense.

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:03.702
No one actually
has an Applebee's

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:04.871
in their neighborhood.
At the very least,

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:07.540
it should be "eatin' good
by the off-ramp."

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.775
You know, last I checked,
you can't buy a house

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.910
in a cozy little cul-de-sac
in suburban New Jersey

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.480
that just happens to be
right next to an Applebee's.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.116
Look, the problem is, though,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.852
Applebee's execs keep telling me
my slogan doesn't work

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.687
because they don't have
jalapeño poppers

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:23.222
and that I should talk
to Arby's.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.490
And, honestly, I don't know the
difference between those two.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.826
I live in Manhattan.
My local neighborhood restaurant

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.794
is a bodega where you can get
an egg and cheese

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.596
on a roll with a side
of AA batteries

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.164
and a single roll of Charmin.

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:34.533
Now, that's eatin' good
in the neighborhood.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.603
What was I saying?
Oh, Biden and Putin.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:40.606
Anyway, Biden was clearly aware
of the potential perils

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.175
of a joint press conference
with Putin.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:45.544
For one thing, he apparently
consulted some Russia experts

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:47.146
who worked for Trump back then

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:49.815
and were horrified by that
press conference in Helsinki.

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:51.684
-Tonight, Axios reporting

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:54.520
the team preparing the President
for the Putin meeting

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.256
includes a group
of outside Russia experts,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.525
including former
Trump officials.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.594
Said to be among the dozen
or so participants --

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:04.130
Fiona Hill, the former

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.098
Trump National Security Council
official

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:09.334
who testified at his
first impeachment trial.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.503
-I just want to read something
that you told the BBC

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:14.006
about the Trump-Putin
press conferences in Helsinki.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.407
And you said this --
You said,

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:18.344
"My initial thought was just,
'How can I end this?'"

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:21.280
Did you seriously consider
that it was that bad?

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.182
-I did seriously think about it.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.817
I, first of all, you know,
looked around

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:27.019
to see if there was
a fire alarm.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:30.055
But, you know, we were
in a rather grand building

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:33.726
attached to the presidential
palace of the Finnish president,

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.828
who had lent it to us
for the occasion.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:38.164
And I couldn't see anything
that resembled a fire alarm.

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:40.766
-It would take more than
a fire alarm to drown out Trump.

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:42.835
The guy spent four years
giving press conferences

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.636
next to a whirring
helicopter blade.

00:06:44.636 --> 00:06:47.373
Second, buildings in Finland
don't have fire alarms?

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:50.042
Do they just, what,
wait for a brigade of gnomes

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:53.412
to come down from the mountains
and put the fire out with magic?

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:55.981
"I heard there was a fire.
Don't worry.

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:59.852
I'll summon a giant wave

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:03.155
with my mystical power!

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:06.125
And if that doesn't work, I'll
smother it with my beard."

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:10.229
Yeah, I think I had it.

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:12.197
That's how bad
the Trump-Putin summit was.

00:07:12.197 --> 00:07:14.767
So Biden has been trying
to learn the lessons

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.702
of that disaster
and avoid any pitfalls.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:19.305
For example, you might remember
this infamous moment

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:21.473
when Trump seemed
to take Putin at his word

00:07:21.473 --> 00:07:23.676
that Russia had nothing to do
with election hacking,

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:27.513
then had to walk it back with
an absolutely absurd excuse.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:30.416
-I have President Putin.

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:32.185
He just said it's not Russia.

00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:35.688
I will say this -- I don't see
any reason why it would be.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:38.357
In a key sentence in my remarks,

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:42.328
I said the word "would"
instead of "wouldn't."

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:45.431
The sentence should have been,
"I don't see any reason

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:49.068
why I wouldn't
or why it wouldn't be Russia."

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:52.405
-It's totally different.
Does that sound familiar to you?

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:55.174
-Uh, like, it goes, "Ding, ding,
ding, diggy, ding, ding.

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:56.842
Ding, ding, ding,
diggy, ding, ding."

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.143
That's the way their's goes.

00:07:58.143 --> 00:08:00.245
Our's goes, "Ding, ding,
ding, diggy, ding, ding, tch.

00:08:00.245 --> 00:08:01.847
Ding, ding, ding,
diggy, ding, ding."

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:04.183
That little bitty "ting,"
it's not the same.

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:06.452
-Did you guys think we wouldn't
play that clip again?

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.920
Now, some of you might
be wondering, "Hey,

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.422
how can you not have the money
to play an MC Hammer sample

00:08:10.422 --> 00:08:12.724
but you do have the money to
play an 'Ice Ice Baby' sample?"

00:08:12.724 --> 00:08:14.793
Well, the answer is because
the "Ice Ice Baby"

00:08:14.793 --> 00:08:16.095
is within the body
of an interview,

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.830
which means it's fair game,
and it also means

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.564
that if we had
MC Hammer on our show

00:08:19.564 --> 00:08:21.766
and we convinced him to say
"you can't touch this,"

00:08:21.766 --> 00:08:23.368
we'd be in the clear,

00:08:23.368 --> 00:08:25.571 line:0%
in a plan we're calling
Operation Work Around,

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:27.572 line:0%
A.K.A.
"you can touch this."

00:08:27.572 --> 00:08:29.208 line:0%
Anyway,
what was I talking about?

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.309
Oh, right, foreign affairs.

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:31.810
And then the moment came
where Biden

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:33.746
finally met Putin face-to-face
as President,

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:36.415
first with an introduction
by the president of Switzerland

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:39.451
and then with a brief handshake
before heading inside.

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:41.454
-Mr. President
of the Russian Federation,

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:43.889
Mr. President of
the United States of America,

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:45.892
on behalf of
the Swiss government,

00:08:45.892 --> 00:08:49.027
I would like to welcome you
to Geneva, the city of peace.

00:08:49.027 --> 00:08:51.330
It is an honor and a pleasure
for Switzerland

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.866
to host you here for this summit

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:56.969
and, in accordance with its
tradition of good officers,

00:08:56.969 --> 00:09:00.238
promote dialogue
and mutual understanding.

00:09:00.238 --> 00:09:03.442
I wish you both presidents
a fruitful dialogue

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:06.444
in the interest of your
two countries and the world's.

00:09:06.444 --> 00:09:08.681
Best wishes, and goodbye.

00:09:08.681 --> 00:09:11.417
[ Camera shutters clicking ]

00:09:16.955 --> 00:09:18.724
-Man, the president
of Switzerland

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:21.861
got the hell out of there
as fast as he could.

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:24.697
"Best wishes and goodbye"
is like the most crushing thing

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:27.599
you can write in someone's
high school yearbook.

00:09:27.599 --> 00:09:29.835
In fairness, if you were
standing between
Putin and Biden,

00:09:29.835 --> 00:09:31.304
you'd be eager
to get out of there, too.

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:33.672
It's like being a referee
at a Tyson fight.

00:09:33.672 --> 00:09:34.940
"All right, gentlemen,
shake hands,

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.141
and let's have
a good, clean fight.

00:09:36.141 --> 00:09:39.912
And if you need me,
I'll be in my car."

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:41.847
This summit was obviously tricky
for many reasons,

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:43.115
because on the one hand,

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:44.750
Biden wants to hold
Putin accountable

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.086
for things like cyberattacks
on critical infrastructure,

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:48.988
human rights abuses,
the killing and jailing

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:50.756
of dissidents,
and election hacking.

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:53.758
And he also wants to stand up
for the principles of democracy.

00:09:53.758 --> 00:09:56.595
But on the other hand, the last
thing anyone should want

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:57.796
is a tense confrontation

00:09:57.796 --> 00:09:59.599
with a nuclear armed country
like Russia.

00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:01.967
We need accountability
and diplomacy.

00:10:01.967 --> 00:10:03.369
Both things can be true
at the same time.

00:10:03.369 --> 00:10:04.904
No one wants another Cold War.

00:10:04.904 --> 00:10:07.640
For one thing, I'm not even sure
30 Rock has a fallout shelter.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:09.341
And if it does,
it's probably crammed full

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:11.744
of old Rock Center
Christmas trees.

00:10:11.744 --> 00:10:13.345
I mean, they can't just
put them out on the curb

00:10:13.345 --> 00:10:15.046
like everyone else.

00:10:15.046 --> 00:10:16.982
Also, I'm not sure
I can duck under this desk,

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:18.851
even if I had to.
For a while during the pandemic,

00:10:18.851 --> 00:10:20.719
I tried sleeping under there,
but I ended up

00:10:20.719 --> 00:10:22.254
just crashing on the sofa,

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:23.689
using cue cards as blankets --

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:26.291
cue cards Wally then
made me pay for.

00:10:26.291 --> 00:10:28.260
-Hey, they don't grow on trees,
Seth.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.696
-Well, they're made out of
paper. They are trees.

00:10:30.696 --> 00:10:33.165
-You know what they say?
"Cicada," "cicawda."

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:36.902
What? Anyway, the two sides
also went into this

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:38.738
clearly aware that there was
a lot to get done

00:10:38.738 --> 00:10:40.038
and not much time to do it.

00:10:40.038 --> 00:10:42.007
In fact, the meeting
only lasted about three hours.

00:10:42.007 --> 00:10:44.810
But originally, U.S. officials
said, "They expected the talks

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.179
to last four to five hours,
or perhaps longer.

00:10:47.179 --> 00:10:49.148
The leaders are not expected
to share a meal."

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:50.449
"No breaking of bread,"

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.217
a senior administration official
said.

00:10:52.217 --> 00:10:54.686
Four or five hours
without a meal?

00:10:54.686 --> 00:10:55.988
Is this a diplomatic meeting,

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:58.023
or are they prepping
for a colonoscopy?

00:10:58.023 --> 00:11:00.059
I mean, Jesus,
if I had to go that long

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:02.728
without so much as a snack,
even I would be screaming.

00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:06.198
-What happened to the server?
Where is the server?

00:11:06.198 --> 00:11:08.267
-Seriously, after four
or five hours without food,

00:11:08.267 --> 00:11:10.436
I think I'd be ready to just say
"[bleep] it" and declare war.

00:11:10.436 --> 00:11:12.337
For the sake of world peace,

00:11:12.337 --> 00:11:15.107
at least get these guys some
crackers and a dip or something,

00:11:15.107 --> 00:11:18.277
or perhaps might I suggest
some jalapeño poppers?

00:11:18.277 --> 00:11:19.578
Only at Applebee's.

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:22.080
I got to get my pop on.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.149
It's good in this neighborhood.

00:11:24.149 --> 00:11:25.851
You could do both.

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.619
And if you thought the meeting
would be tense by the end,

00:11:27.619 --> 00:11:29.688
it was somehow chaotic
from the start,

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:31.724
with reporters jostling
to shout questions

00:11:31.724 --> 00:11:33.359
and get photos
of the two leaders

00:11:33.359 --> 00:11:34.727
sitting next to each other.

00:11:34.727 --> 00:11:36.995
In fact, the audio was so bad,
no one could hear them.

00:11:36.995 --> 00:11:39.931
And at one point, a photographer
blocked everyone's shot

00:11:39.931 --> 00:11:41.867
and refused
to get out of the way.

00:11:41.867 --> 00:11:44.703
-Not in front of the camera.
-I'm not in front of the camera.

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:47.173
-Sir, can you --

00:11:49.808 --> 00:11:51.677
Can you move because
we can't get a shot?

00:11:51.677 --> 00:11:54.847
-I can't do this.
-I told you, go away, please.

00:11:54.847 --> 00:11:57.182
-I can't move because --
-Go away.

00:11:57.182 --> 00:11:58.484
Go away.

00:11:58.484 --> 00:12:00.319
I ask you, go away, please.

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:01.920
-That was one of
the most anticipated

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.421
international summits in years,

00:12:03.421 --> 00:12:05.924
and the press treated it like
an aunt taking a family picture

00:12:05.924 --> 00:12:07.392
with her thumb over the camera.

00:12:07.392 --> 00:12:10.128
"Jesus Christ, Deborah,
let me do this.

00:12:10.128 --> 00:12:11.630
What is this, an Android?

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:14.132
Will someone answer
the damn door?"

00:12:14.132 --> 00:12:15.667
I mean, seriously, dude,
what are you doing?

00:12:15.667 --> 00:12:18.604
You can't just stand in front
of the camera like that.

00:12:18.604 --> 00:12:20.406
You're supposed to be
television professionals,

00:12:20.406 --> 00:12:22.508
and you can't even
get a clean shot?

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:24.343
I mean, we need to see
what's going --

00:12:24.343 --> 00:12:26.145
Sorry.

00:12:26.145 --> 00:12:28.881
Wally, can you -- can you
get out of the way, buddy?

00:12:28.881 --> 00:12:31.082
Wally?

00:12:31.082 --> 00:12:32.851
Wally, you're in the shot.

00:12:32.851 --> 00:12:36.454
No, buddy, that's worse.
See, now you're even closer.

00:12:36.454 --> 00:12:37.623
Wally, come on.

00:12:37.623 --> 00:12:39.558
Wally, I know you're
doing this on purpose.

00:12:39.558 --> 00:12:41.894
I promise next time
a guest drops out,

00:12:41.894 --> 00:12:43.328
you can be the fill-in.

00:12:43.328 --> 00:12:46.165
-"Cicada," "cicawda."

00:12:46.165 --> 00:12:48.500
-What are you talking about?

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.268
Things got so chaotic,
reporters were actually

00:12:50.268 --> 00:12:51.770
pushing and shouting,

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.839
and a lot of them
couldn't even get into the room.

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:55.774
-You saw how chaotic
it was there

00:12:55.774 --> 00:12:57.576
as it was just going on,

00:12:57.576 --> 00:12:59.244
where the reporters
and the cameras are in the room,

00:12:59.244 --> 00:13:01.179
and you could see reporters
blocking the camera,

00:13:01.179 --> 00:13:02.514
people talking to each other.

00:13:02.514 --> 00:13:04.282
We're told it actually
got incredibly tense

00:13:04.282 --> 00:13:06.084
between the two different
press corps,

00:13:06.084 --> 00:13:08.020
which we should note are
separated on the grounds here.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.388
We have the White House
press corps,

00:13:09.388 --> 00:13:11.624
the American press corps,
and the Russian press corps.

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.225
And we're told there were
some combative exchanges

00:13:13.225 --> 00:13:14.493
with the Russian press.

00:13:14.493 --> 00:13:16.328
There was pushing
and there was shoving

00:13:16.328 --> 00:13:17.796
trying to get into that room.

00:13:17.796 --> 00:13:20.499
There was pushing and shoving
and yelling happening outside

00:13:20.499 --> 00:13:23.201
as all of these reporters
were trying to get inside.

00:13:23.201 --> 00:13:24.870
-Oh, my God, is this
a diplomatic meeting

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.104
or a Metallica concert?

00:13:26.104 --> 00:13:28.240
These two dudes,
they're the last guys

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.975
I'd expect
to inspire a mosh pit.

00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:31.910
Although, given his
working-class roots,

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.979
I'm guessing Joe Biden
was in his fair share

00:13:33.979 --> 00:13:35.614
of scuffles back in the day.

00:13:35.614 --> 00:13:37.549
This thing sounded like
a dive bar in Scranton.

00:13:37.549 --> 00:13:39.251
I'm shocked Joe wasn't holding

00:13:39.251 --> 00:13:41.053
half a broken beer bottle
in his hand.

00:13:41.053 --> 00:13:42.821
"We can either head home
to our own beds

00:13:42.821 --> 00:13:43.989
or spend the night in the ER.

00:13:43.989 --> 00:13:45.490
Your choice."

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.960
Right before we stopped
writing this segment

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.628
so I could spend
the rest of the day

00:13:49.628 --> 00:13:52.598
watching Finnish YouTube clips
to nail that accent,

00:13:52.598 --> 00:13:55.500
it should be noted I haven't
been paying my YouTube bills,

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.871
so I think I got
some pretty bad video.

00:13:58.871 --> 00:14:00.840
Both leaders held
their solo press conference.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.374
Putin was asked
if he could achieve

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:04.143
a new level of trust with Biden,

00:14:04.143 --> 00:14:06.144
and his answer was not
exactly reassuring.

00:14:06.144 --> 00:14:08.547
-We just wonder to what extent

00:14:08.547 --> 00:14:12.084
you have now got to
a new level of trust.

00:14:14.319 --> 00:14:18.023
Do you think that,
at this present stage,

00:14:18.023 --> 00:14:23.162
we can talk about a new stage
of bilateral relations?

00:14:24.863 --> 00:14:27.466
There is no happiness in life.

00:14:27.466 --> 00:14:30.703
There's only a mirage
on the horizon.

00:14:30.703 --> 00:14:33.105
So, you know, cherish that.

00:14:33.105 --> 00:14:37.076
-I guess we found a worse thing
to write in someone's yearbook.

00:14:37.076 --> 00:14:40.078
I mean, Jesus, if I had known
that was going to be the answer,

00:14:40.078 --> 00:14:42.614
they could have had Werner
Herzog do the translation.

00:14:42.614 --> 00:14:47.252
"There's no happiness,
only a mirage on the horizon

00:14:47.252 --> 00:14:51.957
as time fades away
and the clock ticks away --

00:14:51.957 --> 00:14:54.659
ticktock, ticktock."

00:14:54.659 --> 00:14:56.929
By the way, I could have also
done it as Christoph Waltz

00:14:56.929 --> 00:14:58.597
and it would have been
very different.

00:14:58.597 --> 00:15:00.365
If it was Christoph Waltz,
he'd be pulling leather gloves

00:15:00.365 --> 00:15:02.001
off his hand
one finger at a time

00:15:02.001 --> 00:15:04.736
while taunting James Bond
about torture.

00:15:04.736 --> 00:15:09.308
"You will soon discover, James,
there's no happiness in life.

00:15:09.308 --> 00:15:12.745
Only a mirage on the horizon,
yes?"

00:15:16.515 --> 00:15:20.218
No one?
No one will back me up? Ice?

00:15:20.218 --> 00:15:21.754
-It's not the same.

00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:23.355
-What? Ice?

00:15:23.355 --> 00:15:25.557
You're gonna do me like that?

00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:27.459
This was perhaps
the most anticipated meeting

00:15:27.459 --> 00:15:28.693
of Biden's presidency so far,

00:15:28.693 --> 00:15:30.696
and it was
a careful balancing act,

00:15:30.696 --> 00:15:32.864
holding Putin accountable
for his actions

00:15:32.864 --> 00:15:34.299
while also pursuing diplomacy

00:15:34.299 --> 00:15:36.268
instead of confrontation
with a nuclear power.

00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:38.971
And you can tell from Biden's
expression that he was ice-cold.

00:15:38.971 --> 00:15:41.006
They might have well played this
during the meeting.

00:15:41.006 --> 00:15:42.908
-"Ding, ding, ding,
diggy, ding, ding.

00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:44.743
Ding, ding, ding, diggy,
ding, ding."

00:15:44.743 --> 00:15:46.211
-What does that even mean,

00:15:46.211 --> 00:15:48.513
going to the well
one too many times?

00:15:48.513 --> 00:15:51.550
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.886 line:0%
♪♪

00:15:54.886 --> 00:15:56.722
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:15:56.722 --> 00:15:58.256
over two million meals a year

00:15:58.256 --> 00:16:00.859
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:16:00.859 --> 00:16:02.527
cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:16:02.527 --> 00:16:03.995
and they need your help now
more than ever.

00:16:03.995 --> 00:16:06.565
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:16:06.565 --> 00:16:09.335
Stay safe, get vaccinated.
We love you.

